{"id":"20260829T005448.077675630Z-372672f2","time":"2026-08-29T00:54:48.07767563Z","session_id":"session-20260829T003802.236153648Z","task_id":"task-1787963882236621025","source":"reviewer","kind":"output","summary":"{\"decision\":\"revise\",\"summary\":\"REVISE. Sensei’s current critical invariant says “Shared context explains why a change was asked for and never enlarges what may be changed.” The initial confinement check is correctly placed for the worker-produced diff, but validation mutates the candidate via formatter(s) and re-reads the diff. An unplanned formatter-created path can therefore reach validation evidence, audit, classification, review, and admission without confinement.\",\"instructions\":\"In internal/workflow/engine.go, call confineToPlannedFiles(diff, tc.Files) again immediately after e.validate returns its re-read diff and before ValidationRun or any downstream inspection/audit/classification/review. Add an end-to-end test using a formatter that writes an unnamed path and prove refusal names that path.\",\"findings\":[{\"id\":\"f1\",\"severity\":\"blocking\",\"claim\":\"The candidate asserts that the pre-validation confinement check ensures no downstream consumer sees a wider candidate.\",\"reference\":\"internal/workflow/engine.go: runCandidate, immediately after e.validate(ctx, ...) returns\",\"reason\":\"e.validate runs mutating formatters and deliberately re-reads the diff afterward. The initial check binds only the worker’s original bytes; a formatter can add or modify an unnamed file, and the returned diff is then consumed downstream unchecked. This violates Sensei invariant sensei_code.workflow.context_never_widens_worker_scope.\",\"correction\":\"Reapply confineToPlannedFiles to the diff returned by e.validate before emitting ValidationRun and before prospective/test-edit inspection, audit, Level-1 classification, review, or admission.\",\"proof_gap\":\"The added tests exercise helper-level diff shapes and source ordering only; none executes the validation path with a formatter that widens the candidate after the first check.\"}]}","payload":{"stream":"stdout"}}
