t the engine's live grants were derived from."},{"id":"f2","severity":"major","claim":"'before anything downstream has read the candidate: validation, the audit, the Level-1 classification, the reviewer and admission all see only a candidate that stayed inside its plan, or they see none' (new comment at engine.go), and the testedit.go doc comment's 'nothing downstream ... is ever handed a wider change than the one that was planned'.","reference":"internal/workflow/engine.go:1248-1257 (comment) and internal/workflow/testedit.go (confineToPlannedFiles doc comment), against engine.go:4393-4402 (e.validate runs the mutating formatter and re-reads via repo.CandidateDiff) and internal/config/config.go:205 (default Format is `gofmt -w cmd internal`)","reason":"e.validate returns a NEW diff read after `gofmt -w cmd internal` has rewritten the candidate worktree; CandidateDiff → CandidateCapture(base, nil) re-runs `add --intent-to-add .` and diffs the whole tree, so any file the formatter rewrote — including one the plan never named, e.g. a file left unformatted at the base or reformatted by a newer gofmt — enters the diff AFTER the confinement check has already run. That post-validate diff is what the audit (engine.go:1328), classifyForDarkRun (1420), the reviewer, EvidenceSnapshot.ChangedPaths (1389) and publication (788 → publish.Open, which commits exactly those paths) all consume. The check is a real boundary on the worker's diff, which is what the architect intent asks for; the comment asserts a containment over validation, admission and publication that the code does not hold, and the ordering assertions in TestCandidateWiderThanPlanIsRefusedBeforeReview (source-text index comparisons) are read as proving it.","correction":"Narrow both comments to what is proven — the worker's diff is confined — and state the residual explicitly: the diff is re-read after the mutating formatter and that re-read is not confined. Do not add a second check here; that is a behaviour change the supplied plan excludes, so name the residual for the architect instead of quietly closing it.","proof_gap":"Nothing in the candidate or the validation evidence tests the post-validate diff against the plan's files; the 'RefusedBeforeReview' test proves only textual ordering inside engine.go."},{"id":"f3","severity":"minor","claim":"plannedOrNone: 'A plan that names nothing authorizes nothing, and saying so is the answer.'","reference":"internal/workflow/testedit.go (plannedOrNone) and internal/workflow/engine.go:1248","reason":"With tc.Files empty, every changed path is outside the plan, so the first non-empty candidate ends the task with a terminal error. Nothing upstream requires a non-empty file list for a modify plan — authority.go:414 raises the coverage gap only `if coverageAbsent \u0026\u0026 len(action.Files) != 0`, and coverageAtWorld simply returns false for an empty list — so an architect decision with no `files` reaches runCandidate today and previously proceeded to validation and review. The fail-closed reading is defensible, but it is a new terminal behaviour introduced by this candidate and the plan said 'no other behaviour changes', with no test pinning it.","correction":"Add the empty-plan case to TestCandidateWiderThanPlanIsRefusedBeforeReview (a plan naming no file refuses any changed path, and the refusal says the plan names '(no file)'), so the intended fail-closed reading is evidence rather than a comment.","proof_gap":"No test covers planned == nil / empty, which is the one input where this check refuses everything."},{"id":"f4","severity":"minor","claim":"The new function is the repository's answer to 'which changed paths did the plan not name'.","reference":"internal/workflow/testedit.go (confineToPlannedFiles) vs internal/workflow/routine.go:290-303 (notPlanned, used by classifyRoutine step 8 at routine.go:256)","reason":"Two representations of the same predicate now disagree. notPlanned compares raw TrimSpace strings over shape.Paths